id: research
name: Research
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Knowledge
requiresSkill: knowledge
requiresRanks: 2
sessionLimit: 1
timeCost: 2 Hours
# "Select a topic." Asked when it is used, and named on the card.
asksTopic: true
# The Check is rolled from the sheet, at the Difficulty the ARC picks there; what is learned is theirs.
effectNote: makes a Knowledge Skill Check at a Difficulty Category the ARC decides (rolled from the sheet) - succeeding gives information on that subject that can prove helpful; failing gives relatively useless information that may hint towards a clue or may not
source: Core Rule
description: >
  Two hours with the books on a topic: a Knowledge Check at the ARC's Difficulty - helpful information
  if it is made, something that may or may not hint at a clue if not.
text: >
  Research: You hit the books, determined to learn something that may help with your current
  predicament.
  –Prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Knowledge
  –Session Limit: 1
  –Time Cost: 2 Hours
  –Effect: Select a topic. Make a Knowledge Skill Check with a Difficulty Category decided by your ARC.
  If you succeed, you gain information on that subject that can prove helpful to your current
  circumstance. If you fail, you gain relatively useless information that may hint towards a clue, or
  may not.

---

# Offered on the Adventure tab to whoever has 2+ Ranks in Knowledge. The topic is asked when it is
# used, and the card names it; once the two hours are spent the card says the Check is owed - rolled
# from the sheet, where the Difficulty the ARC decides is picked - and what each outcome gives, which
# the ARC tells.
